# mports recipe: Angband 4.2.6. Tier 3 item #15 of
# docs/PORTABILITY_HOMEBREW_SNAPCRAFT_ASSESSMENT.md: "Same class [as NetHack],
# cleaner licence, and it has a long history of non-curses frontends, which
# lowers the risk if #2 [ncurses] slips." ncurses landed (userland/ports/
# ncurses), so this is the second real consumer of it after ncurses's own test
# program, and the first real exercise of mports' cross-port `needs=` ordering
# on a shipping port rather than the self-test's synthetic pair.
#
# WHY build=objects, NOT build=script. Angband ships a real ./configure
# (configure.ac + autogen.sh), but nothing it would probe needs a genuine
# autotools run: without HAVE_CONFIG_H, src/h-basic.h SELF-DETECTS a generic
# Unix target (`#define UNIX`, HAVE_STAT, HAVE_FCNTL_H, HAVE_MKDIR all follow
# automatically from "not WINDOWS/GAMEBOY/NDS"), which is exactly the
# environment a cross build without a working `configure` link-test needs.
# src/Makefile.src's ANGFILES0+ZFILES lists are a fixed, versioned object
# list (not autotools-generated), so `sources=` below is that list read
# straight off Makefile.src, plus buildid.c (deliberately NOT part of
# ANGFILES0: see `ANGFILES = $(ANGFILES0) buildid.o`), main.c, main-gcu.c
# (the GCU/ncurses frontend; SYS_x11/SYS_sdl/SYS_sdl2/SYS_stats/SYS_spoil are
# all left out, per docs/PORTABILITY_HOMEBREW_SNAPCRAFT_ASSESSMENT.md section
# 2.6, "no X11, GTK, Qt, or SDL"), and our own mayteraos-curses-compat.c (see
# the patch below).
#
# THREE REAL GAPS THIS PORT FOUND AND CLOSED, in order of how they surfaced:
#
# 1. main.c requires UTF-8: `if (setlocale(LC_CTYPE, "")) { if
#    (!streq(nl_langinfo(CODESET), "UTF-8")) quit(...); }`. userland/libc had
#    setlocale() (locale.h/.c) but no <langinfo.h> at all (a MEASURED absent
#    header per the assessment's section 2.2). Added userland/libc/langinfo.h
#    + langinfo.c to the SHARED libc per docs/MPORTS.md owner rule 1: any
#    future setlocale()+nl_langinfo() idiom (the standard UTF-8-detection
#    idiom in a huge fraction of ported C programs) hits this identically.
#    nl_langinfo(CODESET) honestly returns "UTF-8": this is not a locale claim
#    (locale.h is explicit MayteraOS has exactly one locale, the C locale) but
#    a transport-encoding one, and the terminal's real encoding IS UTF-8
#    (term_parse.c is a real VT220/xterm-class parser that maps DEC
#    special-graphics to Unicode, and text is rendered through antialiased
#    TrueType glyphs, not an 8-bit bitmap font).
# 2. z-file.c's file_lock()/file_unlock() build a `struct flock` and call
#    fcntl(F_SETLKW/F_SETLK, ...) unconditionally under `#if
#    defined(HAVE_FCNTL_H) && defined(UNIX)` (both true here) and NEVER CHECK
#    THE RETURN VALUE (advisory locking is best-effort even on real POSIX).
#    userland/libc/fcntl.h had no lock constants or `struct flock` at all.
#    Added them for SOURCE COMPATIBILITY only: MayteraOS has no multi-process
#    advisory record locking (matching the O_EXCL gap the assessment's 2.5
#    already recorded), so fcntl.c forwards these commands to SYS_FCNTL like
#    any other, the kernel does not recognise them, and every caller in the
#    tree already ignores the return value. Same honest single-writer
#    contract as the SQLite port's custom VFS decision.
# 3. main.c calls `umask(0)` unconditionally before create_needed_dirs().
#    Added `mode_t umask(mode_t)` to userland/libc/sys/stat.h + sys/stat.c:
#    process-local bookkeeping only, since MayteraOS's mkdir()/open(O_CREAT)
#    apply the caller's explicit mode directly with no mask consulted
#    anywhere in the kernel path, so there is nothing for a "real" umask to
#    mask; storing/returning the previous value keeps the POSIX read-back
#    contract without pretending to enforce a kernel behaviour that does not
#    exist.
#
# THE ONE REAL BLOCKER, AND THE PATCH THAT ANSWERS IT. main-gcu.c's ONLY
# glyph-drawing function, Term_text_gcu(), calls mvwaddnwstr() UNCONDITIONALLY
# (there is no narrow-curses fallback left in this Angband version; the
# `-lcurses -ltermcap` line in Makefile.std is vestigial and no longer
# compiles against a real narrow curses). mvwaddnwstr is an ncursesw
# (wide-character) entry point, and userland/ports/ncurses is deliberately
# built --disable-widec ("the emulator and this milestone are 8-bit/UTF-8-
# passthrough"). Rebuilding a second, wide copy of ncurses for one caller
# would be a disproportionate answer: with no tile graphics (USE_GRAPHICS
# off), every glyph the GCU frontend ever draws is a plain code point under
# 256. patches/0001 adds src/mayteraos-curses-compat.{h,c} (FIRST-PARTY
# MayteraOS glue inside the fetched tree, same shape as
# userland/ports/musl-regex/patches/0004's gnuregex.h/gnu_compat.c: one copy,
# where the one copy belongs) implementing mvwaddnwstr on top of the narrow
# waddch() our libncurses.a actually has, and patches main-gcu.c to include
# its header. mvwaddnwstr is listed in `symbols=` below, so a patch that stops
# applying fails the build loudly instead of shipping a binary that cannot
# link.
#
# RUNTIME DATA PATH. Angband needs its lib/ tree (edit files, help text,
# screens, customize/prefs) on disk at ANGBAND_DIR_* paths computed from
# DEFAULT_CONFIG_PATH/DEFAULT_LIB_PATH/DEFAULT_DATA_PATH (src/config.h),
# overridden below to "/ANGBAND/" (mirrors upstream's own default of pointing
# all three at one "./lib/" tree). build/build-golden.sh overlays the
# read-only lib/ tree onto ext2 /ANGBAND, parallel to the existing /TERMINFO
# overlay for mports ncurses.
#
# THE SAVE/SCORE/PANIC PATH IS NOT "~/.angband", AND THIS WAS MEASURED, NOT
# ASSUMED. -DUSE_PRIVATE_PATHS keeps save/score/panic out of the shared
# read-only /ANGBAND tree; the upstream UNIX default for WHERE (PRIVATE_
# USER_PATH="~/.angband") resolves through z-file.c's real
# getpwuid(getuid())->pw_dir (userland/libc/pwd.c reads /CONFIG/PASSWD; not a
# stub), which is elegant and per-user WHEN /CONFIG/PASSWD exists. MEASURED
# on golden 2414 booted with NO first-boot setup wizard run yet (no
# /CONFIG/PASSWD on disk at all, the normal state before OOBE completes): the
# tilde expansion has no passwd entry to resolve against and quietly produces
# a mangled path, and Angband's own create_needed_dirs() then fails outright
# with "Cannot create '<mangled path>'" before the game ever starts. Every
# shipped image bottoms out at this state until OOBE runs, so the elegant
# per-user answer is not a safe DEFAULT.
#
# PRIVATE_USER_PATH is therefore overridden below to the fixed, absolute
# "/GAMES/ANGBAND" (no tilde, no getpwuid dependency), the same
# machine-wide-writable-directory shape as the existing NetHack/SimCity
# entries in kernel/fs/perms.c's perms_shared_state_seed[] table (this port
# adds the matching "/GAMES/ANGBAND" 0777 row there) and build-golden.sh
# creates the directory on ext2, same as GAMES/NETHACK. HONEST LIMIT: this is
# a SINGLE SHARED save location, not per-user; per-user isolation via
# %HOME%/GAMES/ANGBAND (the users_make_home_skeleton() pattern SimCity's
# per-user half uses) is a documented follow-up once every shipped image is
# guaranteed to have completed OOBE.
#
# VERIFIED END TO END with the getpwuid failure reproduced and then routed
# around: on a throwaway VM (golden 2414, pre-OOBE), Angband failed exactly
# as measured above with the tilde-based default; pointed at a machine-wide
# 0777 directory (proven with the ALREADY-SEEDED /GAMES/SIMCITY as a stand-in,
# since the running kernel predates this port's new perms.c row), Angband's
# own create_needed_dirs() succeeded, and the game reached its splash screen,
# then interactive race/class character-creation menus, with keyboard input
# live-updating the displayed stats. The shipped "/GAMES/ANGBAND" row takes
# effect on the next kernel build; the MECHANISM is proven, not assumed.
name=angband
version=4.2.6
class=C
homepage=https://rephial.org/

# The git tag source archive (angband/angband is the canonical upstream repo;
# rephial.org is the project's site, which links there). No separate release
# tarball is published for 4.2.6 beyond OS-specific binaries (osx .dmg,
# windows .exe), matched by checking the GitHub release assets directly at
# port time. sha256 below is of THIS file, MEASURED on the build container:
#   wget -O angband-4.2.6.tar.gz \
